                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14644439" author="dmagda" created="Tue, 28 Jul 2015 14:28:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Pavel, do you have a test or sample code that reproduces the NPE? How frequently does it happen on your side?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14645762" author="pkonstantinov" created="Wed, 29 Jul 2015 09:15:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I do not have any test or code to reproduce that NPE. I got that NPE absolutely randomly. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14645816" author="dmagda" created="Wed, 29 Jul 2015 09:56:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The fix is trivial. The code has to check a client message worker on &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; before working with it. The worker may be null if a client is disconnected before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So what was done:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;checking on &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;throwing an IgniteSpiException if a worker is &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;No need to perform a TC run. Ready for review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14647652" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 30 Jul 2015 13:56:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Did a TC run, everything is OK.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14649052" author="yzhdanov" created="Fri, 31 Jul 2015 10:42:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;merged&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
